---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Applied Social & Qualitative Research"
  description="Interviews, participatory methods and mixed-methods field research for development and value-chain programmes."
>
  <section class="section service-page">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow"><a href="/#what-we-do">&larr; What We Do</a></p>
      <h1>Applied Social &amp; Qualitative Research</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Numbers tell you what changed. Social research tells you why, and
        for whom. We run interviews, focus groups and participatory research
        that surface the lived experience behind a programme&rsquo;s
        indicators.
      </p>

      <div class="body-grid">
        <div>
          <h2>What this covers</h2>
          <p>
            Qualitative and mixed-methods research design, field interviews,
            focus group discussions and participatory methods with
            communities, workers and local partners. Much of our work sits in
            fragile, culturally diverse and sensitive settings: artisanal
            mining communities, smallholder value chains, and places where
            language, custom and local power dynamics shape what people are
            willing to share and with whom. Reading these environments and
            building the trust to work in them well is one of our particular
            strengths.
          </p>
          <p>
            We also carry out stakeholder mapping and consultation processes
            for organisations that need to understand a local context before
            designing a project. This groundwork often shapes the project
            design itself, well before any evaluation begins.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h2>How we work</h2>
          <p>
            Research stays grounded in the realities of the communities and
            partners involved. We adapt tools to language, culture and
            context, and stay careful about consent, safeguarding and how
            findings involving real people are handled and shared.
          </p>
          <p>
            Findings feed directly into the frameworks and reporting our
            MEAL work produces, keeping research insight embedded in the
            material programme teams actually use.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="pill-btn" href="/contact">Talk to us about your research needs</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .service-page .eyebrow {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .service-page .eyebrow a {
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  .lede {
    max-width: 720px;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    margin-bottom: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);
  }

  .body-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--gap);
    margin-bottom: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4rem);
  }

  .cta-row {
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(40, 40, 40, 0.1);
    padding-top: 2rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 800px) {
    .body-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
